# E2E Tests Directory

This directory contains all end-to-end tests for the Skills Manager application.

## Directory Structure

```
e2e/
├── fixtures/          # Test data and fixtures
│   └── test-skills/   # Sample skill packages for testing
├── helpers/           # Test helper functions
│   └── tauri-helpers.ts
├── pages/             # Page Object Models (POM)
│   ├── base.page.ts
│   ├── my-skills.page.ts
│   ├── marketplace.page.ts
│   └── settings.page.ts
└── specs/             # Test specifications
    ├── skill-management.spec.ts
    ├── skill-import.spec.ts
    ├── security.spec.ts
    ├── sharing.spec.ts
    └── settings.spec.ts
```

## Running Tests

```bash
# Run all E2E tests
npm run e2e

# Run tests in UI mode (recommended for development)
npm run e2e:ui

# Run tests in debug mode
npm run e2e:debug

# View test report
npm run e2e:report
```

## Writing Tests

1. Add `data-testid` attributes to UI elements for stable selectors
2. Use Page Object Models to encapsulate page interactions
3. Write descriptive test names that follow the pattern: "should [expected outcome]"
4. Use `test.describe()` to group related tests
5. Use `test.beforeEach()` for common setup

## Test Guidelines

- Keep tests independent and isolated
- Use explicit waits with `waitFor` instead of fixed timeouts
- Mock external dependencies (file dialogs, network requests)
- Clean up test data after each test
- Add comments for complex test logic
